---
// Experience: the job list and the LinkedIn link under it. Used on Home and About.
// Each page adds its own "experience" heading and the space around the list.
import Job from './Job.astro';
---

<div class="jobs">
  <Job
    title="Senior product designer"
    meta={['Authentic Digital (client: Calastone)', 'Nov 2021 - present, full-time', 'Remote from Poland, UK company']}
  >
    <p>
      B2B SaaS for Calastone, the transaction network the global funds industry runs on, used by fund operations
      teams at end clients including HSBC, Federated Hermes, and Allspring.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Sole designer on ETF Servicing since late 2022, and moved into the lead designer role on Money Market
        Services after it started in 2024, owning design decisions across a stakeholder group of PMs, product
        owners, business analysts, product directors, and engineering.
      </li>
      <li>
        Drove a rebuild of the design system behind both products instead of forking it: a Figma variable and
        token architecture carried into the Angular build through per brand config, taking 6 brand tenants to
        zero forked libraries and reducing a new tenant launch to a token change.
      </li>
      <li>
        Mapped the domain before any UI existed, with flow charts, BPMN, and process diagrams, then designed the
        primary ETF create and redeem workflow HSBC uses across management entities in Europe and Asia: order
        capture, pricing, settlement, and registry reconciliation against depositories including TA2000.
      </li>
      <li>
        Designed four eyes approval by running working sessions with client operations teams on how approvals
        actually moved in their firms, then iterating review states until they matched; the client signed off
        the final process.
      </li>
      <li>
        Crafted high fidelity UI for the order detail view, the product's core operating surface: charge
        amendments, prefunding and settlement dates, and a full audit log, dense enough for expert operators,
        still legible, and forgiving of mistakes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Delivered WCAG AA across the shared design system ahead of the April 2026 ADA Title II deadline,
        testing every component with an accessibility specialist engineer: keyboard navigation, WAVE, and NVDA
        screen reader passes before sign off.
      </li>
      <li>
        Drove new work on Money Market Services including the bulk multi trading flow, an inline form table for
        large trade batches; met AA on keyboard, ARIA, contrast, and font scale, documented the screen reader gap
        as an explicit tradeoff, and put it on the roadmap.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Job>

  <Job
    title={['Senior product designer,', 'then art director']}
    meta={['Juicyway', 'Aug 2021 - Feb 2024, contract', 'Remote from Poland, Nigeria based company']}
  >
    <p>
      Consumer and B2B fintech in Nigeria, through several pivots. Sole designer at first, later directing a
      small brand and motion team.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Built a design foundation that bent with the strategy through every pivot: colour, typography,
        iconography, imagery tiers, and a component set that became the substrate for the shipped Juicyway
        platform, whose customers include Bolt, Technogym, and Nigerian Breweries.
      </li>
      <li>
        Ran each pivot as design and prototype before engineering committed, so the company could test a direction
        without spending a build cycle on it; those prototypes were what went in front of investors.
      </li>
      <li>
        Moved into art direction as the brand and motion team formed, setting creative direction, running design
        reviews, and translating the CEO's vision into what the product shipped
      </li>
      <li>
        Shipped across web dashboards, web apps, and Flutter mobile, embedding in backend standups so product and
        UX decisions fed directly into build scope.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Job>

  <Job
    title="Product UX and UI designer"
    meta={['VisualPanda (main client: Bamboo)', 'Mar 2018 - Dec 2021, full-time', 'Remote from Poland, Nigerian client']}
  >
    <p>
      External product designer embedded in client teams. Main engagement: Bamboo (Jan 2020 - Aug 2021), a
      mobile investing app letting Nigerian users buy US stocks, mutual funds, and fractional shares with dollars
      converted from naira.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Ran a discovery phase the engagement had no budget for, producing personas, user stories, and competitor
        analysis with support from the client's UX researcher, which became the basis for the product roadmap.
      </li>
      <li>
        Launched Bamboo on iOS and Android as sole product designer, covering the full product surface: mobile
        apps, web app, internal admin panels, and marketing site, roughly 500 artboards, and working through
        implementation on interactions, gestures, and animations.
      </li>
      <li>
        Rebuilt onboarding with KYC, identity verification, bank linking, and source of funds as the spine of the
        flow rather than an obstacle added on top, for users new to investing.
      </li>
      <li>
        Built the case for the one year redesign by pairing the client's external UX audit with an independent UI
        audit and customer support signals, writing a screen by screen proposal and presenting key screens for
        client sign off; shipped a new brand, dark mode, and rebuilt data visualisation.
      </li>
      <li>
        Designed for the low specification Android hardware common in the market, simplifying data visualisation
        so one chart read for both novice and expert investors.
      </li>
      <li>
        Additional engagements: Helium Health (Y Combinator backed Nigerian health tech), DrOnline (US and UAE
        health tech), DoubleMap (US transportation).
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Job>

  <div class="more">
    <p>See more at my</p>
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/zastawny/">LinkedIn</a>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* 44px between the jobs, no lines between them */
  .jobs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 44px;
  }

  /* "see more at my LinkedIn": 60px below the last job (90px on mobile) */
  .more {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* A glass pill like the nav, so the keyboard focus ring sits around the button, not the whole row */
  .more a {
    align-self: center;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 56px;
    padding: 0 32px 2px; /* the font sits low in its box: 2px at the bottom centres the letters */
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--glass-sheen-top), var(--glass-sheen-bottom)),
      var(--glass-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-rim);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 var(--glass-highlight),
      inset 0 -1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.05),
      inset 0 0 16px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(160%) brightness(0.7);
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(160%) brightness(0.7);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-in-out);
  }

  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .more a:hover {
      color: var(--color-accent-2);
      background-color: var(--glass-active);
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Mobile ---------- */
  @media (max-width: 799.98px) {
    .more {
      padding-top: 46px;
    }
  }
</style>
